# Treeloom simple deployment — copy to .env, add your key, run ./run-simple.sh
# (see docs/simple-mode.md). The profile defaults everything else: embedded
# LanceDB vectors (~/.treeloom/lancedb), embedded SQLite graph
# (~/.treeloom/graph.db), OpenAI embeddings + gpt-4o-mini for HyDE/summaries.
# Reranking: a CPU cross-encoder out of the box, but if you add a rerank key
# below it auto-upgrades to that cloud reranker (GPU-parity, no GPU). Any var
# you set here overrides a profile default.

TREELOOM_PROFILE=simple
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Recommended: GPU-parity reranking (just add a key) -------------------
# Adding any ONE of these auto-switches reranking to that cloud provider —
# Cohere rerank-v4.0-pro was the best-measured (beats the GPU stack). No GPU,
# sub-second. See the table in docs/simple-mode.md.
# COHERE_API_KEY=...        # -> cohere rerank-v4.0-pro (recommended)
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=...        # -> voyage rerank-2.5
# ZEROENTROPY_API_KEY=...   # -> zerank-2

# --- Optional overrides ---------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoints (separate keys via EMBEDDING_API_KEY/LLM_API_KEY):
# EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# Best CPU reranker if you stay GPU-less AND keyless (slow: ~16s/query):
# RERANKER_LOCAL_MODEL=jinaai/jina-reranker-v2-base-multilingual
# Enable per-chunk LLM summaries + the summary hybrid leg (costs LLM calls
# per indexed chunk):
# USE_SUMMARY_VECTOR=1

# MCP access is stdio by default (treeloom-mcp, no container). Uncomment to
# also start the deprecated HTTP+SSE mcp-server container (docs/simple-mode.md):
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=http-mcp
